
/.idea
/ignore experimental
# TODO: Duplicate entries - /ignore_experimental appears twice
# WHY: Lines 4 and 5 are identical, creating redundant ignore rules.
# FIX: Remove one of the duplicate /ignore_experimental lines.
/ignore_experimental
/ignore_experimental
# TODO: Overly broad pattern may break build process
# WHY: *.json ignores ALL JSON files, but main.spec (line 7) requires accounts.json, config.json,
# and login_credentials.json to exist at build time. If these files are not tracked (or template versions
# are not committed), PyInstaller builds will fail. Also prevents committing a requirements or package.json if needed.
# FIX: Use more specific patterns like /accounts.json, /config.json, /login_credentials.json instead of *.json,
# or commit empty template versions of these files.
*.json
# TODO: Overly broad pattern ignores required Chrome/ChromeDriver executables
# WHY: *.exe ignores all executables, but the application depends on chrome/chrome.exe and chromedriver/chromedriver.exe
# (referenced at lines 28-29 in main.py and included in main.spec line 7). If these are ignored, the application
# cannot function and builds will be incomplete.
# FIX: Use specific patterns like /*.exe or /dist/*.exe to ignore build outputs only, and explicitly track
# chrome/chrome.exe and chromedriver/chromedriver.exe with negation patterns: !chrome/chrome.exe, !chromedriver/chromedriver.exe
*.exe
# TODO: Overly broad pattern may ignore important documentation files
# WHY: *.txt ignores all text files, potentially including requirements.txt (Python dependencies),
# documentation files, licenses, or other important project files.
# FIX: Use more specific patterns or track requirements.txt explicitly with !requirements.txt
*.txt
/codstatus_env
# TODO: Ignoring /chrome directory conflicts with application requirements
# WHY: The application requires chrome/chrome.exe (main.py line 28, main.spec line 7), but this line
# ignores the entire chrome directory. This creates a conflict where the app needs the directory
# but git ignores it, making distribution impossible without manual setup.
# FIX: Either remove this line and track chrome/ with proper .exe handling above, or document that
# users must manually download and place Chrome in this directory.
/chrome
/build
